    "$comment": "Content addressing. A CID names a record by hashing it, so the same record has the same name everywhere and an altered record has a different name than the one anybody cited. Layered so that nothing is agreed out of band: multibase `b` (base32, lower case, unpadded), then CIDv1 (0x01), then the codec dag-cbor (0x71), then the multihash sha2-256 (0x12) with length 32 (0x20), then the digest. `cid` is the CID of `value` encoded as DAG-CBOR — so an implementation that fails these while passing encoding/dag-cbor.json has its hashing or its prefixes wrong rather than its encoder.",
